= Non-Reimbursable Expenses & Prohibited Items

== Master Disallowed Expense Catalog

The company will not reimburse expenses deemed personal, excessive, or unrelated to legitimate corporate operations. The following list represents common non-reimbursable categories:

#policy-warning("POL-NON-001", "Fines, Penalties & Legal Citations")[
  All traffic fines, speeding tickets, parking violations, toll violation fees, late payment charges, credit card interest fees, and banking overdraft charges incurred during business travel are the exclusive responsibility of the employee and will not be reimbursed under any circumstance.
]

#policy-warning("POL-NON-002", "Personal Grooming, Health & Apparel")[
  The following items are non-reimbursable:
  - Personal grooming services, haircuts, manicures, massages, saunas
  - Clothing, suits, shoes, luggage, bags, umbrella purchases
  - Over-the-counter medications, health club / gym access fees
  - Personal toiletries (toothpaste, shaving kits) unless replacing lost luggage during verified airline transit delays exceeding twenty-four (24) hours
]

#policy-warning("POL-NON-003", "Gift Cards, Upgrades & Family Travel")[
  - *Gift Cards*: Purchases of retail gift cards, prepaid debit cards, or digital vouchers
  - *Companions*: Travel, meal, or lodging costs for spouses, children, partners, or pets
  - *Upgrades*: Paid upgrades for airline cabin classes, hotel suites, or rental car premium tiers
  - *Personal Subscriptions*: Streaming services (Netflix, Spotify), newspaper home deliveries, or entertainment subscriptions
]
